      en: "The Seven Sisters Falls is a series of seven waterfalls located within the Grand Etang National Park in central Grenada. The falls are fed by the Grand Etang Lake outflow. The highest cascade plunges approximately 30 meters (98 feet). The entire system descends over a distance of about 500 meters (1,640 feet) along a rocky gorge. The trail to the falls is 1.5 km (0.9 miles) one way, passing through lush cloud forest. The first fall is the most accessible, while the upper falls require scrambling. The area receives over 3,000 mm of rain annually. The water is clear and cool, averaging 22°C (72°F). The site is managed by the National Parks Authority.",
